{"id":"code-dedupe","title":"Remove duplicates, keep order","category":"code","difficulty":1,"prompt":"Write a Python function `dedupe(items: list) -> list` that returns a new list with duplicates removed, keeping the first occurrence of each item in its original position. The input list must not be modified. Items are hashable.","system":"You are completing one task from an evaluation suite. Do the task as asked.\n\nReply with one Python code block that defines exactly what the task asks for. Use only the standard library. Do not include tests, examples, or print statements.","grader":{"type":"code","entrypoint":"dedupe","tests":["assert dedupe([]) == []","assert dedupe([1, 2, 1, 3, 2]) == [1, 2, 3]","assert dedupe([\"b\", \"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"a\"]) == [\"b\", \"a\", \"c\"]","assert dedupe([3, 3, 3]) == [3]","x = [3, 3, 1]; dedupe(x); assert x == [3, 3, 1]"]},"reference":"```python\ndef dedupe(items: list) -> list:\n    seen = set()\n    out = []\n    for item in items:\n        if item not in seen:\n            seen.add(item)\n            out.append(item)\n    return out\n```","answers":["```python\ndef dedupe(items: list) -> list:\n    seen = set()\n    out = []\n    for item in items:\n        if item not in seen:\n            seen.add(item)\n            out.append(item)\n    return out\n```","```python\ndef dedupe(items: list) -> list:\n    return sorted(set(items))\n```"],"cells":[{"arm":"haiku-low","trial":0,"mode":"sync","status":"ok","score":1.0,"passed":true,"answer":0,"details":{"passed":5,"total":5,"tests":[{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true}],"simulated":{"pass_probability":0.979,"answer":"reference"}},"input_tokens":145,"output_tokens":124,"cost_usd":7.65e-05,"latency_ms":981.7},{"arm":"haiku-low","trial":1,"mode":"batch","status":"ok","score":1.0,"passed":true,"answer":0,"details":{"passed":5,"total":5,"tests":[{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true}],"simulated":{"pass_probability":0.979,"answer":"referen